Kind: widen
Issue: #617
Holds open: a thread ending through the full pool, between giving its stack back and thread_terminate() -- it waits 100 ms there, and pthread_test's full-pool case creates nine threads meanwhile, the ninth taking a stack from free_stacks; with the fix in, the ending thread's stack waits on dying_stacks for its port to die and the ninth gets another, with the fix out the ninth gets that stack while the thread is still on it; each wait says so on the console that needs no lock, so that a fixed run that passes shows the window was open; at most 64 waits in a task
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/lib/libpthreads/pthread.c b/uros/src/lib/libpthreads/pthread.c
index 7d17d2b6..af23271e 100644
--- a/uros/src/lib/libpthreads/pthread.c
+++ b/uros/src/lib/libpthreads/pthread.c
@@ -1184,6 +1184,33 @@ _pthread_run_thread_cleanup(pthread_t self)
 	mig_dealloc_reply_port(MACH_PORT_NULL);
 }
 
+/*
+ * ablations/617-widen-stack-given-back.patch: #617's widened window, and not
+ * an ablation.  A thread ending through the full pool waits WIDEN_617_MS
+ * between giving its stack back and thread_terminate(), so that a
+ * pthread_create() meanwhile meets it: with the fix in, the stack waits on
+ * dying_stacks for the thread's port to die and the new thread gets another;
+ * with the fix out it is on free_stacks, the new thread gets it, and the
+ * ending thread returns through its frames.  Said on the console that needs
+ * no lock, so that a fixed run that passes shows the window was open.  At
+ * most WIDEN_617_TIMES in a task.
+ */
+#define	WIDEN_617_MS		100
+#define	WIDEN_617_TIMES		64
+
+static int	widen_617_waits;	/* a budget, not a census */
+
+static void
+widen_617_given_back(void)
+{
+	if (widen_617_waits >= WIDEN_617_TIMES)
+		return;
+	widen_617_waits++;
+	mach_print("#617 widen: a thread ending through the full pool waits "
+		   "100 ms between giving its stack back and thread_terminate()\n");
+	(void) thread_switch(MACH_PORT_NULL, SWITCH_OPTION_WAIT, WIDEN_617_MS);
+}
+
 void 
 pthread_exit(void *value_ptr)
 {
@@ -1261,6 +1288,7 @@ pthread_exit(void *value_ptr)
 		return;		/* NOT REACHED — park loops into trampoline */
 	/* Pool full — actually terminate, on a stack still ours (#617) */
 	me = _pthread_free_own_stack(self);
+	widen_617_given_back();
 	MACH_CALL(thread_terminate(me), kern_res);
 
 	/*
